    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 13 • 7:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-white-oryx/paragraph-13.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 13 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "Abdullah takes its head in his hands. The little oryx opens its eyes and moves its legs. “No, it’s OK.” Abdullah smiles. “But its mother is dead,” Mandy says. “Can it live?” “Yes,” Abdullah says. ’It’s young, but it isn’t a baby. We can find it a new mother. No problem.’ “Wait,” Mandy says suddenly. ’I want some photos.’"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
